# Story 11: Tab Mode (Ctrl+T) (45s)
# Hook: Ctrl+T opens tab mode -- create, jump, and move between tabs without leaving the keyboard.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-011-tab-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Ctrl+T opens tab mode -- create, jump, and move between tabs without leaving the home row.

[00:05.0 --> 00:18.0]
Press Ctrl+T to enter tab mode. Now n creates a new tab. Press it a few times to build out a row of tabs.

[00:18.0 --> 00:30.0]
While in tab mode, h and k move to the previous tab, j and l move to the next -- no arrow keys needed.

[00:30.0 --> 00:40.0]
Press a number from 1 to 9 to jump straight to that tab.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Escape exits tab mode and drops you back to normal mode.

